{
  "profile": "HCPQ v1",
  "description": "Canonical TransactionBody encoding vectors. A node accepts HCPQ-signed bodyBytes only when they are byte-for-byte the canonical encoding of the parsed TransactionBody.",
  "format_version": 1,
  "notes": [
    "body is the SignedTransaction.bodyBytes value in lowercase hexadecimal.",
    "accept: body is the canonical encoding. body_json is the same TransactionBody in the proto3 JSON mapping, so an SDK can build it and compare bytes. transaction_digest is the HCPQ transaction digest of body under ledger_id.",
    "reject: a conforming node rejects any transaction carrying an HCPQ signature over body. rejected_by is strict_parse when strict parsing fails (malformed data, unknown fields, invalid UTF-8) and canonical_reencode when body parses but its canonical encoding differs.",
    "equivalent_to names the accepted test whose TransactionBody the rejected bytes parse to. Those bytes are an alternate encoding of the same value."
  ],
  "tests": [
    {
      "id": "crypto_transfer",
      "comment": "Baseline HBAR transfer. sint64 amounts use ZigZag encoding.",
      "result": "accept",
      "body": "0a0f0a080880e2cfaa06107b120318e907120218031880c2d72f2202087832046863707172160a140a080a0318e90710c7010a080a0318ea0710c801",
      "body_json": {
        "transactionID": {
          "transactionValidStart": {
            "seconds": "1700000000",
            "nanos": 123
          },
          "accountID": {
            "accountNum": "1001"
          }
        },
        "nodeAccountID": {
          "accountNum": "3"
        },
        "transactionFee": "100000000",
        "transactionValidDuration": {
          "seconds": "120"
        },
        "memo": "hcpq",
        "cryptoTransfer": {
          "transfers": {
